# No CI — by design

This repository is a **download-only template**. It is never deployed, built,
or published — people clone it and initialize a knowledge base in their own
project. There is nothing to ship, so **CI is intentionally disabled.**

Do **not**:

- rename `.github/workflows/ci.yml.disabled` to `ci.yml` / `*.yaml`,
- create any new `.github/workflows/*.yml` or `*.yaml`,
- add Travis/CircleCI/other CI config,
- "fix" the absence of CI in any other way.

GitHub only runs workflows matching `*.yml` / `*.yaml`; the only workflow file
here ends in `.disabled`, so nothing runs. **Keep it that way.**

Run checks locally instead:

```bash
pytest
```

If a task seems to require CI, it almost certainly does not for this repo —
leave CI off and do the equivalent work locally.
